# How to Write a New Article

## 1. Create the file

Add a new `.md` file inside `content/ideas/`:

```
content/ideas/your-article-title.md
```

Use lowercase with dashes, no spaces (e.g. `why-ai-wins.md`).

---

## 2. Add the frontmatter

Every article must start with this at the top:

```
---
title: Your Title Here
date: YYYY-MM-DD
---
```

---

## 3. Writing format

**Subtitle / intro line** — wrap in `*italics*`:
```
*This is the subtitle or one-liner under the title.*
```

**Bullets** — start each line with `- `:
```
- First item
- Second item
- Third item
```

**Horizontal divider** — use `---` on its own line:
```
---
```

**Image** — place where you want it to appear:
```
<div class="article-image-wrap">
  <img src="your-image-filename.jpg" alt="Description" class="article-img-small" />
</div>
```
Drop the image file into `content/ideas/` and use the exact filename.

**Bold text** — wrap in `**double asterisks**`:
```
**This is bold**
```

---

## 4. Add it to the Ideas index

Open `content/ideas/index.md` and add a new card block:

```
<a class="idea-card" href="/ideas/your-article-title">
  <div class="idea-card-text">
    <div class="idea-title">Your Title Here</div>
    <div class="idea-date">Month DD, YYYY</div>
  </div>
  <img class="idea-image" src="/ideas/your-image-filename.jpg" alt="Your Title" />
</a>
```

Paste it inside the `<div class="idea-grid">` block, above the existing cards.

---

## 5. Restart the server to see changes

```
npx quartz build --serve
```
